<article class="env-lemma" id="0GU7">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0GU7">Lemma <span data-tag="0GU7">42.22.3</span>.</a> Let $(S, \delta )$ be as in Situation <a href="/tag/02QL" data-tag="02QL">42.7.1</a>. Let $X' \to X$ be a morphism of schemes locally of finite type over $S$. If $f : Y \to X$ is an envelope, then the base change $f' : Y' \to X'$ of $f$ is an envelope too. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      Follows from Morphisms, Lemma <a href="/tag/01W4" data-tag="01W4">29.42.5</a> and More on Morphisms, Lemma <a href="/tag/0GTK" data-tag="0GTK">37.78.3</a>. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>